@startuml
title ProofSieve | Integrate a verification endpoint
hide footbox

actor "API caller" as Caller
participant "Keycloak" as KC
participant "ProofSieve Guard" as Guard
participant "Configured check\nservice" as Check
database "Decision\nevidence" as Evidence

opt Keycloak service account is configured
    Caller -> KC: Request a token via client credentials
    KC --> Caller: Access token with the API audience\nand the endpoint role
end
note over Caller
  A configured opaque ProofSieve
  bearer token is also supported.
end note

opt Discover and try permitted endpoints
    Caller -> Guard: GET /openapi.json with bearer token
    Guard --> Caller: Contract scoped to the caller's grants
    note over Caller, Guard
      Swagger UI on the operator listener uses this contract
      to show request examples and send explicit test calls.
    end note
end

Caller -> Guard: POST to the selected /verify path with bearer and data\nInclude operationId in decision mode
Guard -> Guard: Authenticate and authorize the exact path
alt Invalid token or missing grant
    Guard --> Caller: HTTP 401 or 403
else Ordinary verification with a stale If-Match
    Guard --> Caller: HTTP 412 · reload the rule before retrying
else Authorized
    Guard -> Guard: Load the saved rule and input profile
    alt JSON facts or RDF Turtle
        Guard -> Guard: Use JSON for ODRL or Turtle for SHACL
    else SD-JWT VC, mdoc IssuerSigned or W3C VC
        Guard -> Guard: Verify issuer signature and integrity\nwith configured trust
    else Document signatures or seal
        opt Local check enabled for this profile
            Guard -> Guard: Verify document signatures locally
        end
        opt External check enabled for this profile
            Guard -> Check: Send required check data\nfor DSS or another configured check
            Check --> Guard: Check result or status
            Guard -> Guard: Validate and bind result to the input
        end
    else Proof bundle
        Guard -> Guard: Verify each configured input and check\ncross-proof and operation bindings
    end
    Guard -> Guard: Evaluate the saved rule when checks pass\nOtherwise derive refusal or indeterminate
    alt Recorded decision mode
        Guard -> Evidence: Record operation, rule version,\ncaller, outcome and check evidence
        alt Evidence stored
            Evidence --> Guard: Decision ID
            Guard --> Caller: Recorded outcome with decision ID
        else Evidence unavailable
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
        end
    else Boolean, Guard or URL mode
        Guard --> Caller: Result in the configured mode
    end
end

opt Decision recorded and export enabled on the operator listener
    Caller -> Guard: GET /evidence with the same caller,\nendpoint and operationId\nOptional decisionId selects one record
    Guard -> Evidence: Read scoped evidence and sign the export
    Guard --> Caller: Signed JSON decision evidence
end

legend bottom
  |= Response mode |= Typical result |
  | Boolean | HTTP 200 with true or false |
  | Guard | HTTP 200 for approval or 403 for policy refusal |
  | URL | JSON decision and optional return or fail URL for the caller to use |
  | Decision | Outcome, operation ID, decision ID and rule version. HTTP 503 if indeterminate |
  | Decision with forwarding | See approved-forwarding-flow.puml for delivery outcomes |
  | Wallet presentation | See wallet-evidence-flow.puml for start, completion and recovery |
endlegend
@enduml
